course: dictionary
lesson: 12541
title: Deter: stopping someone from acting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To deter someone is to make them decide not to do something. It often works by making them worried about what will happen next. «The big sign and the tall fence deter people from climbing into the old factory.» The sign and fence do not hold anyone back by force. They make people think twice and choose not to climb.
explain: Deter can also mean to make something less likely to happen. «The smell of lemon deters ants from the kitchen.» The ants do not want to come near the smell, so they stay away. Ask yourself: what might happen without the thing in the sentence?
explain: Watch for the phrase «not be deterred». «Heavy rain did not deter the children from playing football.» The rain could have stopped them, but they played anyway. Not being deterred means carrying on, even when there is a reason to stop.
fact: Deter is a verb: deter, deters, deterred, deterring.
fact: «Deter» means to make someone decide not to do something, often by making them afraid of what will happen.
fact: «Deter» can also mean to make something less likely, like a smell that deters insects.
fact: Signs, fences and cameras are used to deter crime.
fact: «Not be deterred» means keep going even when something could stop you.
exercise: «The big sign and the tall fence deter people from climbing into the old factory.» What does deter mean here? | To paint the sign bright red | To build a fence around a factory | To make people climb faster | * To stop people from wanting to climb in, by making them think twice
exercise: «Heavy rain did not deter the children from playing football.» What does this tell you? | * The children kept playing even though it rained | The rain was warm and sunny | The children stopped as soon as it rained | The children did not like football
exercise: Which word means to make someone decide not to do something? | Decorate | Donate | Describe | * Deter
test: «Cameras in the car park deter thieves.» What does deter mean here? | Chase thieves away with a loud noise | * Make thieves less likely to steal | Help thieves park their cars | Show thieves the way out
test: Ellie says, «Nothing could deter me from finishing the marathon.» What does Ellie mean? | She is running very slowly | She will stop running as soon as it gets hard | She has never run before | * She will finish, however hard it gets
exam: «The scary dog sign was meant to deter people from opening the gate.» What was the sign's job? | To show people where the gate is | * To make people less likely to open the gate | To make the gate look newer | To tell people the dog's name
